#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
me.py — SecuriFi firmware CLI (adapted from ESPectre's ./me tool)

Handles flashing the CSI-enabled MicroPython firmware and deploying/running
the SecuriFi master/slave node code, matching this repo layout:

Securi-Fi_Node/
├── me.py                      <-- this file lives HERE (repo root)
├── grapher.py
├── venv/
├── firmware/                  <-- downloaded/cached .bin files (auto-created)
├── slave_node/
│   ├── shared/
│   │   ├── csi_capture.py
│   │   ├── mq2.py
│   │   ├── mvs_detector.py
│   │   ├── securifi_node.py
│   │   └── traffic_generator.py
│   └── slave/
│       ├── config.py
│       ├── main.py
│       ├── slave_node.py
│       └── node_id.txt
└── master_node/
    ├── shared/  (same 5 files as above)
    └── master/
        ├── config.py
        ├── main.py
        ├── master_node.py
        └── node_id.txt

On-device layout produced by `deploy` (for either node type):
    /main.py
    /config.py
    /master_node.py   (or /slave_node.py)
    /node_id.txt
    /shared/__init__.py     <-- generated automatically, makes `shared` a package
    /shared/*.py

This matches the imports used in the code, e.g.:
    from shared.securifi_node import SecuriFiNode, NodeReading
    from config import MQTT_BROKER, ...
"""

